{#
    Cloudflare Turnstile widget for a form written in Twig template mode.

    The SuluFormBundle mode gets its widget from a form field, which a
    hand-written form cannot use: without this partial, the anti-spam field
    shipped by the bundle is simply out of reach in Twig template mode, and the
    project ends up declaring the site key a second time to render its own.

    IMPORTANT - this only renders the widget. Cloudflare answers it with a token
    in the `cf-turnstile-response` field of the POST, and **the project must
    verify that token server-side**: a widget nobody checks stops no robot at
    all. See doc/turnstile.md.

    Renders nothing when the feature is off or unconfigured, so a template can
    include it unconditionally and a missing key never breaks a page.

    Parameters:
      - colorScheme: 'light' | 'dark' | 'auto' - the surface the form sits on.
                     A widget inside an iframe cannot inherit the theme CSS, it
                     only takes a light/dark hint, so pass the block's value
                     straight through.
      - attributes:  optional map of extra data attributes (e.g. { 'data-action':
                     'contact' }), for the Turnstile options this partial does
                     not cover.

    Override it in your project at the standard Symfony bundle path:
    templates/bundles/ItechWorldSuluTailwindThemeBundle/forms/_turnstile.html.twig
#}

{% set siteKey = iw_sulu_tailwind_theme_turnstile_site_key() %}

{# Enabled but unconfigured is the worst of both worlds: no widget, and a
   server-side check that refuses every submission because the token is always
   empty. It only happens once deployed - locally the keys are in .env - so it
   is said out loud in dev rather than left to be discovered in production. In
   prod the same case is logged, see ThemeExtension::getTurnstileStatus(). #}
{% if iw_sulu_tailwind_theme_turnstile_status() == 'missing_key' and app.environment == 'dev' %}
    <p class="iw-block-form__notice">{{ 'iw_sulu_tailwind_theme.turnstile_key_missing'|trans }}</p>
{% endif %}

{% if siteKey is not null %}
    {# `defer`: the script is only needed once the widget is in the DOM, and a
       blocking third-party request in the middle of a page is a needless delay.
       Twig deduplicates nothing here, so a page holding two forms loads it
       twice - the browser serves the second from its cache. #}
    <script src="https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js" defer></script>
    <div class="iw-form__turnstile cf-turnstile"
         data-sitekey="{{ siteKey }}"
         data-theme="{{ colorScheme|default('auto') }}"
         {%- for name, value in attributes|default({}) %} {{ name }}="{{ value }}"{% endfor %}></div>
{% endif %}
